{"name":"Galactic Compass","dev":"Acts Not Facts Ltd","keys":["ios:6451314440"],"ios":{"id":"6451314440","url":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/galactic-compass/id6451314440?uo=4","rating":4.83824,"ratings":68,"price":"Free","genre":"Travel","screens":["https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/PurpleSource211/v4/75/b6/b3/75b6b322-2591-1f8a-3cba-7e7720753f08/c49608d3-47ed-409c-bfb5-752cb5872f0a_photo-cropped-55.jpg/392x696bb.jpg","https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/PurpleSource211/v4/51/81/81/51818189-d84b-e1f4-1cfa-8b41d1916240/a1f7c2cc-99ce-4ae1-b3f5-c872cbbd086d_gc-dark-mode-55.png/392x696bb.png","https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/PurpleSource211/v4/b2/01/c2/b201c232-c3ed-99d2-4c3b-adbfb7bade17/cd810d9a-9f09-4276-aebb-7b588a9c7970_gc-light-mode-55.png/392x696bb.png"],"desc":"Galactic Compass presents you with a floating arrow with one purpose: to point the direction of the central supermassive black hole of the Milky Way galaxy, known as Sagittarius A*.\n\nThe middle of the galaxy is 26,000 light years.. but which way?\n\nThe direction depends on:\n\n- the time of day\n- your location\n- the position of the Earth in its orbit\n\nIt's hard to figure out in your head.\n\nWell now the answer is in your pocket. If you're ever lost, Galactic Compass can show you the way.","released":"2024-02-14","updated":"2026-08-14","icon":"https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Purple211/v4/1a/8f/3c/1a8f3caf-57d4-fcea-b60a-aa9250a779a8/AppIcon-0-0-1x_U007ephone-0-1-85-220.png/512x512bb.jpg","age":"4+"},"android":null,"icon":"https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Purple211/v4/1a/8f/3c/1a8f3caf-57d4-fcea-b60a-aa9250a779a8/AppIcon-0-0-1x_U007ephone-0-1-85-220.png/512x512bb.jpg","cat":"Travel & Maps","rating":4.84,"ratings":68,"mentions":1,"users":1,"threads":1,"hn_points":1,"hn_comments":0,"submissions":1,"self_n":0,"hn_score":3.0,"first":1740228933,"last":1740228933,"show_hn":null,"n_lab":1,"pos_pct":0,"neg_pct":0,"mood":null,"quotes":[{"id":43138601,"k":"ios:645131444